Z||000000||FIEROCIOUS||06-25-2000||01:47 AM||||I was putting the pieces back together on my recently rebuilt 87 GT engine when I noticed that the coolant pipe from the timeing cover has eroaded away and has pits in it!<P>Well, I went to my local GM parts specialist and found that the timeing cover is no longer available!<P>I decided to reuse the original and was scrapeing the gasket material from the waterpump side and noticed it was abnormaly pitted also!<P>Turns out who ever owned the car before me replaced the gasket and removed the old gasket with a grinder yes I said GRINDER! Idiot!<P>So long story short I need a timeing cover or have the one I have milled! <P>What cars/trucks used the same timeing cover? mine uses a one-piece oil pan gasket.<P>Has anyone milled their cover? Did it work?    <P>SCCA Fiero do you have a spare cover?<P>Thanks in advance!!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||06-25-2000||01:50 PM||||Now, I don't know for a fact that all GM 2.8-liter FWD V6 engines (1980- ?)had the same timing cover, but I suspect that most of them are probably similar.  And salvage yards seem to have plenty of X-cars & J-cars available (Citations, Cavaliers, etc.).  Take your pitiful cover with you, to be sure what you pull from the salvage yard, will fit up.     <P>As a matter of fact, when I replaced timing chain on a Fiero earlier this year, I happened to have an old timing cover from a V6 Citation lying around, so I used the old cover as a bolt organizer.  Knew there was SOME reason I hadn't tossed it!<P>Hope this helps you...   ||||reg||3
Z||000002||terryk||06-25-2000||01:54 PM||||Anyone of the 1.2 billion MPFI Celebrity 2.8L MPFI's in the junk yards.<P>Same engine except for a few brackets to make it fit the Fiero and the top plenum, throttle body and MAP (instead of the mass air flow).||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tim||06-25-2000||03:16 PM||||87-88 fiero only,except the 3.4 S-10 crate motor.  Sorry, I'd checked in to the situation a couple of years ago. You will need to buy a used one or repair what you have to keep the one piece oil pan gasket or convert to the earlier oil pan.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FIEROCIOUS||06-26-2000||12:28 AM||||So terry, I (CAN) use a cover from a Celebrity? What years have the one piece oil pan 87-on right?<P>Tim, are you saying 87-88 fiero's have a one of a kind cover? exept for the crate motor? Or the crate motor has the same cover?<P>Any guesses on how much I can mill the cover?<BR>(water pump side)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tim||06-26-2000||10:32 PM||||The crate motor uses the same cover as 87-88 fiero. Yes, 87-88 fieros and the crate motor covers are unique. F-body water pumps run backwards. FWD uses a different pump. <P>Use RTV and the paper gasket on the old cover with the new pump.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FIEROCIOUS||06-28-2000||01:12 AM||||87-93 camaro s10 s15 isuzu pup all use the same cover the part number is differant because of the timeing tab! that is the only differance! <P>Thanks for your help all!||||reg||1
