Z||000014||Fret Naught||07-03-2000||01:01 AM||||This may sound a bit trite, but why not fix your old one?. may take a couple of hours, but get a piece of glass (it is usually realitively flat) start with a sheet of pretty aggressive emery paper say 120 grit and lap the cover. Once is is apparant that you have a continous flat area step up the grits say 220 then 400 wet dry paper, and you are done. We use to do that with our Harly covers all the time. you may need to get a slighly thicker gasket when you are done is all.||||reg||5
